WEBVTT

01:42.268 --> 01:44.187
So, uh, you think you could beat him?

01:44.771 --> 01:47.524
- Who? The caveman?
- Yeah.

01:48.149 --> 01:49.984
Not interested. Sorry.

01:50.485 --> 01:51.945
- But why not?
- Rumina.

01:52.529 --> 01:54.656
This guy, "Pickle,"

01:55.323 --> 01:58.326
he's a priceless
scientific specimen, y'know?

01:59.035 --> 02:02.789
Like a national monument.
Something to be put on display.

02:02.872 --> 02:03.957
[slurps[

02:04.040 --> 02:06.960
Fighting someone like him...

02:07.710 --> 02:11.047
...would be like trying to remodel
one of the pyramids, I don't know.

02:11.131 --> 02:14.676
Everyone says
that he's even stronger than a T. rex.

02:15.343 --> 02:16.970
Yeah, I've heard.

02:19.556 --> 02:21.641
I don't get you, Baki.

02:21.724 --> 02:24.060
You'll fight anything,
even a praying mantis,

02:24.144 --> 02:26.396
but you don't care
about fighting the caveman?

02:26.479 --> 02:28.982
You're right, kid. You don't get me.

02:29.065 --> 02:32.277
I'm not interested in beating
every other fighter in the world.

02:32.777 --> 02:34.779
I'm only interested in beating my dad.

02:35.446 --> 02:38.992
But, man, my dad is just so damn strong...

02:39.075 --> 02:39.909
Hmm.

02:41.077 --> 02:41.995
Hmm?

02:42.579 --> 02:43.997
You're doing it again.

02:44.080 --> 02:46.249
Doing what?

02:47.000 --> 02:49.586
Every time you talk to me
about your dad, Baki,

02:49.669 --> 02:51.004
you look really happy.

02:57.677 --> 02:58.511
Hmm.

02:59.095 --> 03:00.597
I look happy?

03:00.680 --> 03:02.015
You really do.

03:12.192 --> 03:13.193
<i>For Pickle,</i>

03:13.276 --> 03:16.446
<i>there was one thought
he couldn't get out of his primitive mind.</i>

03:17.113 --> 03:19.782
<i>The memory of what had happened.</i>

03:20.491 --> 03:23.244
<i>He could picture
the moment their bodies met.</i>

03:23.328 --> 03:25.705
<i>What puzzled him was what happened next.</i>

03:26.331 --> 03:27.916
<i>That sudden movement.</i>

03:27.999 --> 03:30.710
<i>No opponent had ever done that
to him before.</i>

03:31.878 --> 03:34.214
<i>Not that one, or that one,</i>

03:34.797 --> 03:36.174
<i>or even that one.</i>

03:36.841 --> 03:39.302
<i>Nothing he'd ever faced had done it.</i>

03:40.303 --> 03:42.388
<i>It was an unsolvable riddle,</i>

03:43.014 --> 03:44.807
<i>complicating his simple life.</i>

03:46.017 --> 03:47.560
<i>It made Pickle happy.</i>

03:47.644 --> 03:49.562
KUNG FU TRAINING AND RESEARCH CENTER

03:57.153 --> 03:59.656
Number... ...nine!

04:05.662 --> 04:08.081
He smashed just the ninth one!

04:08.164 --> 04:09.332
Seven!

04:11.668 --> 04:12.835
Four!

04:14.170 --> 04:15.338
Amazing !

04:15.421 --> 04:16.839
Never seen anything like it.

04:16.923 --> 04:18.091
That's precision!

04:20.218 --> 04:21.594
End of demonstration.

04:22.553 --> 04:24.389
Incredible!

04:28.142 --> 04:29.978
That was really impressive.

04:30.061 --> 04:33.982
You could do it, too,
if you just applied yourself.

04:34.065 --> 04:35.108
I dunno.

04:35.692 --> 04:37.735
I'm not too good at the subtle stuff.

04:37.819 --> 04:40.655
So, why have you come today?

04:43.074 --> 04:45.493
You want me to teach you kung fu, then?

04:46.077 --> 04:48.496
Kung fu is such
a treasure trove of principles.

04:49.122 --> 04:50.456
Far as I'm concerned,

04:50.540 --> 04:52.041
you're a great master,

04:52.125 --> 04:53.501
no matter what you've done.

04:54.294 --> 04:56.504
Please? Teach me?

04:56.587 --> 04:57.547
Hmm.

05:01.342 --> 05:02.552
No, I won't.

05:03.344 --> 05:04.554
Frankly,

05:05.263 --> 05:07.265
you don't interest me, Baki.

05:08.349 --> 05:09.183
Why not?

05:09.267 --> 05:10.935
Don't take it personally.

05:11.853 --> 05:15.690
You see, right at this moment,
I am interested in absolutely nothing,

05:16.482 --> 05:17.775
and no one,

05:17.859 --> 05:19.777
other than one person.

05:22.113 --> 05:23.656
You must know who I mean.

05:24.699 --> 05:27.535
This Jurassic man, the caveman.

05:27.618 --> 05:29.579
- Pickle.
- That's right.

05:29.662 --> 05:31.039
<i>Not him again.</i>

05:31.664 --> 05:33.124
But, Retsu, Pickle is a--

05:33.207 --> 05:34.375
Yes, I know.

05:34.459 --> 05:35.543
He is a treasure.

05:36.169 --> 05:37.545
A rare specimen.

05:38.463 --> 05:40.548
I am fully aware of all that!

05:42.133 --> 05:44.510
I know it's madness to fight him.

05:45.261 --> 05:47.430
To even think about wanting to fight him.

05:48.056 --> 05:49.807
But this feeling that I have,

05:49.891 --> 05:51.225
it's like a hunger.

05:51.893 --> 05:54.771
When I have this strong a desire
to fight a man,

05:54.854 --> 05:56.564
it's a lot like love.

05:57.732 --> 05:59.192
I feel I have to know him.

05:59.984 --> 06:01.152
I have to hold him...

06:01.778 --> 06:03.071
Get him in my grip.

06:03.154 --> 06:04.405
It's a passion.

06:05.698 --> 06:08.076
I am burning with a passion
to fight this man,

06:08.743 --> 06:12.080
this embodiment of savagery
from before time.

06:12.747 --> 06:16.167
These skills I have
were developed over 4,000 years.

06:16.834 --> 06:20.588
How will they match up
against the skills of a caveman?

06:22.131 --> 06:24.801
I can't even imagine
the moves he must have.

06:25.468 --> 06:27.220
<i>That's why I want to fight him.</i>

06:27.303 --> 06:28.763
<i>Why I have to fight him!</i>

06:29.555 --> 06:31.724
<i>Unbelievable, I've been dumped.</i>

06:31.808 --> 06:35.061
<i>Pickle, Pickle, Pickle. That's all
anyone cares about these days.</i>

06:35.144 --> 06:37.313
<i>Japan's got Pickle on the brain.</i>

06:38.606 --> 06:41.067
<i>I bet it's a pain for him too. Hmm.</i>

06:51.160 --> 06:54.872
Captain Strydum
and Mitsunari Tokugawa,

06:54.956 --> 06:58.584
thank you both for your concern
and cooperation in this project.

06:58.668 --> 07:01.587
Pickle's wellbeing
is extremely important,

07:01.671 --> 07:05.925
and not just for research scientists
such as yourself, but for all humankind.

07:06.008 --> 07:09.345
So when I hear that he hasn't consumed
anything but water for more than a month,

07:09.429 --> 07:13.224
believe me, I'm fully aware
of the seriousness of the situation.

07:13.933 --> 07:15.852
We've regarded him as an animal,

07:16.436 --> 07:18.521
when, in fact, he is a proud warrior.

07:18.604 --> 07:21.858
A fierce fighter who craves
and thrives on competition.

07:22.692 --> 07:26.362
He won't eat anything
that he hasn't fought and killed himself.

07:26.946 --> 07:28.364
Extraordinary!

07:28.948 --> 07:31.617
He's extraordinary all right.
That's the problem.

07:31.701 --> 07:34.787
<i>We've tried throwing
a Spanish bull in there with him,</i>

07:35.371 --> 07:36.622
<i>a Kamchatka brown bear.</i>

07:36.706 --> 07:37.957
<i>even a lion.</i>

07:38.708 --> 07:40.626
<i>Pickle just sat there.</i>

07:40.710 --> 07:44.130
<i>But they took one look at him,
and ran for the hills.</i>

07:46.215 --> 07:49.635
I've never seen a lion
with its tail between its legs before.

07:50.428 --> 07:54.640
In a war between worlds,
his beats ours without even fighting.

07:54.724 --> 07:56.976
It all comes down to this.

07:57.059 --> 07:59.395
Let's hope it proves a worthy opponent.

07:59.479 --> 08:01.606
Well, we paid enough for it.

08:01.689 --> 08:05.151
But I guess you expect that
when you're buying an endangered species.

08:05.234 --> 08:06.903
I feel bad about it,

08:06.986 --> 08:09.155
but it's for a worthy cause, after all.

08:10.323 --> 08:12.450
It hasn't eaten in five days.

08:12.533 --> 08:14.660
It's primed and ready to go!

08:14.744 --> 08:16.662
The Siberian tiger.

08:16.746 --> 08:19.081
The most powerful of the big cats.

08:19.165 --> 08:24.212
And this one is 4.7 meters long
and weighs 490 kilos.

08:24.295 --> 08:26.047
One of the largest of its kind.

08:26.130 --> 08:30.176
In other words, the most ferocious
fighting beast on the planet.

08:30.259 --> 08:33.679
- It's enormous!
- It's almost as big as the bull!

08:40.520 --> 08:42.230
He's on his feet!

08:42.313 --> 08:45.024
The tiger looks at Pickle as his prey.

08:45.107 --> 08:46.442
Yes, and vice versa.

08:53.533 --> 08:54.450
Hmm?

08:55.535 --> 08:56.452
Huh?

08:58.538 --> 08:59.956
How horrifying!

09:00.540 --> 09:02.208
'Specially for the tiger.

09:02.291 --> 09:04.335
But that's how it is with Pickle.

09:04.418 --> 09:08.214
Anything that attacks him
becomes food in his eyes.

09:08.297 --> 09:10.216
ENDANGERED SIBERIAN TIGER
V CULTURAL ASSET PICKLE

09:19.809 --> 09:24.564
A species on the verge of extinction
has just ended up as a lunchtime snack

09:24.647 --> 09:26.232
for our visiting caveman.

09:26.315 --> 09:28.317
Asked to comment on the controversy,

09:28.401 --> 09:30.736
Professor Albert Payne spoke
earlier today.

09:30.820 --> 09:33.489
I understand that many people are upset,

09:33.573 --> 09:35.700
but the very fact
that Pickle exists at all

09:35.783 --> 09:36.993
is really a miracle.

09:37.076 --> 09:40.746
However, replicating his Jurassic diet
is extremely difficult.

09:40.830 --> 09:41.914
Because of that,

09:41.998 --> 09:45.001
we've had to sit and watch
this miracle man starve to death.

09:45.084 --> 09:46.502
<i>Now, I'm fully aware</i>

09:46.586 --> 09:49.380
<i>that the Siberian tiger
is an endangered species.</i>

09:49.463 --> 09:50.590
But the fact is,

09:50.673 --> 09:53.509
they're the only thing we've found
that Pickle will eat.

09:53.593 --> 09:55.136
So, we can feel sad

09:55.219 --> 09:58.014
that there are only 500
of them left in existence.

09:58.097 --> 10:01.517
But I say we should be grateful
there are still 500!

10:01.601 --> 10:03.936
And if every last one of them
has to be sacrificed

10:04.020 --> 10:07.273
in order to keep Pickle alive,
that's a small price to pay, I say!

10:07.356 --> 10:11.277
After all, a tiger is just a tiger.
Pickle is a one-of-a-kind treasure!

10:11.360 --> 10:14.030
The professor's comments drew
a quick and angry response

10:14.113 --> 10:17.783
<i>from environmentalists
and Animal rights activists everywhere.</i>

10:17.867 --> 10:22.038
<i>Massive protest demonstrations
are being planned by social action groups.</i>

10:22.121 --> 10:25.541
MITSUNARI TOKUGAWA

10:26.959 --> 10:29.503
It seems everybody's
got an opinion on this one,

10:29.587 --> 10:32.214
and the police have
quite a few questions themselves!

10:34.508 --> 10:35.551
Aah.

10:35.635 --> 10:39.305
So, Sea King Retsu,
to what do I owe the pleasure?

10:39.388 --> 10:42.308
You're having trouble
finding food for Pickle?

10:42.391 --> 10:43.976
Mmm.

10:44.060 --> 10:48.064
Finding him food
that isn't an endangered species, yes.

10:48.648 --> 10:50.900
From what I've heard, he'll only eat

10:51.567 --> 10:53.819
an animal that's strong enough
to fight back.

10:53.903 --> 10:56.072
Yes, and that's part of the problem.

10:56.155 --> 10:59.533
These animals must have
some kind of survival instinct.

10:59.617 --> 11:01.535
<i>They take one look at Pickle and flee.</i>

11:01.619 --> 11:03.579
<i>Even the lion turned tail and ran.</i>

11:03.663 --> 11:05.039
- Well, then.
- Huh?

11:05.122 --> 11:07.917
How do you propose
to solve your dilemma, sir?

11:11.253 --> 11:12.755
It's a tricky one.

11:12.838 --> 11:14.715
What do you suggest, Retsu?

11:14.799 --> 11:16.217
Tokugawa,

11:17.093 --> 11:19.220
what if you were to feed me to Pickle?

11:19.303 --> 11:20.137
Huh'?

11:24.058 --> 11:24.975
But, Retsu...

11:25.810 --> 11:28.771
Here he is! Professor Payne,
having been questioned by the police,

11:28.854 --> 11:31.732
is just now coming out
of the Metropolitan Police Department!

11:31.816 --> 11:33.984
How do you respond
to all your critics, sir?

11:34.068 --> 11:36.445
- Nothing to say at this time?
- Is a panda next?

11:36.529 --> 11:38.531
Are you ready? We'll put you on record.

11:41.325 --> 11:43.369
I have come here to offer myself.

11:43.869 --> 11:45.996
Let me be the caveman's prey.

11:46.080 --> 11:47.415
Yes, well,

11:47.498 --> 11:50.501
I'm not sure feeding him a human's
a good idea, Retsu.

11:50.584 --> 11:52.294
But he must be fed.

11:52.378 --> 11:54.296
The professor said it himself,

11:54.380 --> 11:56.507
Pickle's very existence is a miracle.

11:57.174 --> 11:59.093
But letting him eat a human?

11:59.176 --> 12:02.763
We got in enough trouble
feeding him a Siberian tiger.

12:03.347 --> 12:05.766
Good sir, do you really assume

12:06.308 --> 12:08.769
that Retsu would meekly
allow himself to be eaten?

12:08.853 --> 12:10.020
Huh?

12:10.104 --> 12:13.274
Pickle may look upon me
as his prey, but I assure you,

12:14.734 --> 12:17.027
Sea King Retsu is no one's meal.

12:19.113 --> 12:21.031
And it would be quite a match.

12:21.657 --> 12:22.533
Huh?

12:22.616 --> 12:24.827
Pickle versus Sea King Retsu!

12:27.621 --> 12:30.291
What?!
Put a human in there with him?

12:30.374 --> 12:32.042
Are you insane?

12:34.128 --> 12:34.962
Hmm?

12:35.045 --> 12:37.590
We've never felt more sane
in our life!

12:37.673 --> 12:40.050
Besides, the man
freely volunteered for the job.

12:49.059 --> 12:52.563
<i>It's incredible how he can sleep
out in the open like that.</i>

12:52.646 --> 12:56.484
<i>Most animals in the wild find
a secure place to hide themselves in</i>

12:56.567 --> 12:57.818
<i>when they go to sleep.</i>

12:57.902 --> 13:01.280
<i>But he lies there
like he hasn't a care in the world,</i>

13:01.363 --> 13:04.241
<i>even though he's completely defenseless.</i>

13:04.325 --> 13:06.327
<i>Lions on the savanna sleep like that,</i>

13:07.077 --> 13:10.831
<i>so maybe this sense of confidence
comes naturally to Pickle as well.</i>

13:11.499 --> 13:14.794
<i>Only those animals at the very top
of nature's food chain</i>

13:14.877 --> 13:16.504
<i>can afford to sleep that way.</i>

13:16.587 --> 13:18.923
<i>It's the sleeping posture of kings.</i>

13:19.924 --> 13:20.800
<i>But, of course,</i>

13:20.883 --> 13:24.345
<i>the Jurassic world he came from
wasn't as forgiving as the savanna.</i>

13:24.428 --> 13:27.848
<i>It was a world of ceaseless rivalry,
constant danger,</i>

13:27.932 --> 13:29.225
<i>and sudden death.</i>

13:30.184 --> 13:33.604
And yet look at him,
lying there so peacefully.

13:33.687 --> 13:35.064
Yes, exactly!

13:35.147 --> 13:38.859
Why would you wanna let a human
go up against a sleeping killer like that?

13:39.443 --> 13:43.030
Well, for one thing, it should make for
an intriguing match, at the very least.

13:43.113 --> 13:44.031
I agree.

13:44.532 --> 13:47.701
A fight between Pickle's pure,
God-given instincts

13:47.785 --> 13:51.372
and Retsu's mastery of 4,000 years
of kung fu tradition.

13:51.455 --> 13:54.124
<i>This promises to be an epic battle.</i>

13:54.208 --> 13:56.252
Epic massacre, more like!

13:56.335 --> 13:58.254
He'll be eaten a moment after he wal--

13:58.337 --> 14:00.256
Shut up, Professor, will you?

14:02.341 --> 14:03.676
<i>"Shut up"?</i>

14:04.426 --> 14:07.555
<i>Professor Payne had never been told
to "shut up" before.</i>

14:08.138 --> 14:12.101
<i>It was a new and puzzling experience
for this Nobel laureate.</i>

14:12.184 --> 14:13.269
Now, wait a minute.

14:13.352 --> 14:16.480
I really must insist
that you hear me out, gentlemen.

14:17.106 --> 14:20.526
<i>You've seen yourselves
what Pickle can do to an opponent!</i>

14:20.609 --> 14:24.780
No human is a match for that combination
of muscle mass and savagery!

14:34.123 --> 14:36.041
Did I wake him? Was I too loud?

14:36.125 --> 14:39.295
Well, you were a little loud,
but I don't think it was you.

14:40.337 --> 14:42.047
It was something else that woke him.

14:46.135 --> 14:48.304
He's gotten up to meet the foe!

14:48.387 --> 14:50.347
<i>He's never done that before,</i>

14:50.431 --> 14:51.891
<i>not even for the lion!</i>

14:52.641 --> 14:56.562
He must sense
that 4,000 years of kung fu are comin'.

14:57.396 --> 14:58.647
Hai!

14:59.398 --> 15:03.819
<i>The savage man knew at once
he was facing a savagely worthy opponent.</i>

15:05.404 --> 15:08.824
He's really taking up a fighting stance!
Well, that's new.

15:08.908 --> 15:11.327
I'll never get this chance ever again!

15:16.040 --> 15:17.625
For this contest,

15:17.708 --> 15:20.836
I will call upon all my strength
and every skill I have ever learned.

15:22.922 --> 15:25.633
So perhaps I was wrong about this fellow.

15:25.716 --> 15:28.344
I've never seen Pickle
on the defensive before.

15:29.929 --> 15:32.848
Why's he coming closer to him?
What's he doin'?

15:32.932 --> 15:35.142
<i>I'm inside your zone, Pickle.</i>

15:43.192 --> 15:44.193
I knew it!

15:44.276 --> 15:45.903
I knew this wouldn't work!

15:45.986 --> 15:48.113
What'd I tell you?
The man doesn't stand a chance!

15:48.197 --> 15:49.990
Well, one thing's clear.

15:50.699 --> 15:52.868
Sheer strength alone won't cut it.

15:54.244 --> 15:55.871
I'll have to use all my tricks!

15:58.457 --> 15:59.500
Hi-yah!

16:08.217 --> 16:09.259
Hi-yah!

16:10.219 --> 16:12.638
-<i>Is it over?</i>
-<i>Already?</i>

16:14.473 --> 16:15.891
Wait, is Pickle crying?

16:21.730 --> 16:23.857
<i>He took that kick
full in the face.</i>

16:24.400 --> 16:26.402
<i>A normal man would have died.</i>

16:26.485 --> 16:28.654
<i>All he did was fall on his butt.</i>

16:29.446 --> 16:31.156
<i>Well, all I can say to that is...</i>

16:31.740 --> 16:32.616
Well done!

16:42.209 --> 16:43.293
<i>Impossible!</i>

16:43.377 --> 16:45.170
<i>A human overpowering Pickle?!</i>

16:45.254 --> 16:46.171
Huh!

16:52.011 --> 16:53.012
Yah!

16:53.637 --> 16:55.014
<i>Right on the button.</i>

16:56.640 --> 16:59.393
<i>That was six clean blows
straight to the chin!</i>

16:59.476 --> 17:03.022
<i>It's inconceivable the amount
of damage his brain must have suffered.</i>

17:03.772 --> 17:05.357
<i>It should be mush by now!</i>

17:07.026 --> 17:08.777
<i>Ah, such bliss!</i>

17:09.278 --> 17:11.447
<i>Please don't let it be over already!</i>

17:33.052 --> 17:34.470
Pickle bit him!

17:39.558 --> 17:41.727
He's... he's eating him!

17:54.073 --> 17:56.492
My punches have no effect!

17:58.077 --> 18:00.496
That's me he's chewing on!

18:03.999 --> 18:06.502
- A-ha, that means...
- Huh?

18:06.585 --> 18:09.004
He's finally taking the gloves off.

18:09.838 --> 18:13.759
Now, with both his feet and his fists,
he's fighting bare-knuckled.

18:16.345 --> 18:17.846
You bastard.

18:17.930 --> 18:19.264
How dare you eat me...

18:19.348 --> 18:20.766
...and cry!

18:27.356 --> 18:28.774
<i>All my skills,</i>

18:28.857 --> 18:30.818
<i>everything I've learned,</i>

18:30.901 --> 18:33.403
<i>4,000 years of history</i>

18:33.487 --> 18:34.988
<i>have no effect on him!</i>

18:36.115 --> 18:38.325
<i>Is it possible that a world exists</i>

18:38.408 --> 18:40.786
<i>where the martial arts
have become useless?</i>

18:41.954 --> 18:44.581
<i>Then farewell, 4,000 years.</i>

18:44.665 --> 18:46.834
<i>I will abandon all those skills.</i>

18:46.917 --> 18:49.878
<i>If the world has changed, then so will I.</i>

18:50.629 --> 18:52.047
<i>Sea King Retsu.</i>

18:52.131 --> 18:56.802
<i>That was the name given to me by my master
when I was initiated into these arts.</i>

18:56.885 --> 18:58.804
<i>But if I am to save myself,</i>

18:58.887 --> 19:01.807
<i>I must become once again Eishu Retsu,</i>

19:01.890 --> 19:03.642
<i>the name my father gave me!</i>

19:03.725 --> 19:05.394
<i>The name my mother gave me!</i>

19:05.894 --> 19:09.565
<i>Eishu Retsu will save Sea King Retsu!</i>

19:09.648 --> 19:11.984
Hold on. What kind of pose is that?

19:12.067 --> 19:13.068
No idea.

19:13.694 --> 19:15.821
<i>Must swallow my pride.</i>

19:17.656 --> 19:19.324
<i>The windmill punch.</i>

19:19.408 --> 19:23.662
<i>He abandoned all strategy,
tactics, skill, and efficiency,</i>

19:23.745 --> 19:26.373
<i>and instead relied on pure emotion,</i>

19:26.915 --> 19:28.834
<i>channeling his rage into this.</i>

19:28.917 --> 19:33.338
<i>Probably the oldest weapon
of last resort in human history.</i>

19:34.798 --> 19:36.466
<i>But the results were...</i>

19:37.926 --> 19:39.178
You're kidding.

19:39.261 --> 19:41.680
Are those really windmill punches
he's throwing?

19:41.763 --> 19:44.349
What is he,
a five-year-old having a temper tantrum?

19:44.433 --> 19:47.269
[narrator[ <i>For Pickle,
this was very confusing.</i>

19:47.352 --> 19:50.314
<i>He was being attacked,
so of course he fought back.</i>

19:50.397 --> 19:53.108
<i>And when he fought,
he fought with all his strength,</i>

19:53.192 --> 19:55.861
<i>even against an attacker
who was so pathetic.</i>

19:59.698 --> 20:01.617
- He's back to kung fu!
- Aah!

20:04.203 --> 20:07.623
<i>What's wrong with me?
Why did I do that?</i>

20:07.706 --> 20:11.126
<i>I told myself I wasn't going to use
any moves, or tactics,</i>

20:11.210 --> 20:12.628
<i>or skills...</i>

20:16.715 --> 20:18.133
<i>I did it again!</i>

20:25.724 --> 20:27.643
- He's back again!
- Attaboy.

20:27.726 --> 20:29.645
<i>Wha-- What's that?</i>

20:29.728 --> 20:32.439
<i>Retsu... Retsu...</i>

20:33.732 --> 20:35.943
You coldhearted fool.

20:38.570 --> 20:42.199
Why are you so coldhearted, Retsu?

20:45.494 --> 20:47.663
<i>What is this? Who are you?</i>

20:47.746 --> 20:50.165
You don't know?

20:50.249 --> 20:52.668
I am you, Retsu.

20:52.751 --> 20:54.962
Or the you you aim to be.

20:55.504 --> 20:57.673
I am the you that you want to become.

20:58.674 --> 21:01.176
I am <i>the</i> Sea King Retsu.

21:01.260 --> 21:03.679
<i>Is this my ideal self?</i>

21:04.304 --> 21:05.597
I'm disappointed.

21:06.265 --> 21:08.684
You abandoned the martial arts

21:08.767 --> 21:12.187
when you decided to use
the windmill punch in this battle.

21:12.854 --> 21:15.148
But the martial arts didn't abandon you.

21:19.778 --> 21:22.197
You're being tested, Retsu.

21:22.281 --> 21:24.449
You need to trust in yourself.

21:24.950 --> 21:26.702
Forget about shouldering the burden

21:26.785 --> 21:28.495
of 4,000 years of history.

21:29.079 --> 21:30.706
Surrender to your body.

21:31.290 --> 21:32.207
<i>If you do not,</i>

21:32.708 --> 21:37.212
<i>you will never be capable
of shouldering anything ever again.</i>

21:37.296 --> 21:38.714
<i>Ever again.</i>

21:38.797 --> 21:41.049
<i>Trust in myself.</i>

21:44.303 --> 21:47.055
<i>Trust in my martial arts.</i>

21:48.807 --> 21:50.350
<i>Trust in them completely.</i>

21:55.439 --> 21:57.607
<i>Don't doubt yourself.</i>

21:57.691 --> 22:00.986
<i>Have complete faith in yourself.</i>

22:02.070 --> 22:03.488
<i>Entrust everything.</i>

22:03.572 --> 22:04.656
<i>Everything...</i>

22:08.577 --> 22:10.996
<i>...to the bosom of the martial arts.</i>

22:12.080 --> 22:13.582
<i>That's what it means</i>

22:13.665 --> 22:15.459
<i>to shoulder the burden</i>

22:15.542 --> 22:18.253
<i>of 4,000 years of history!</i>
